From 5055356d8abed4b9044bb5d3ae48167bdcafe2ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:24:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v1: sign-in retry, quick launch, a phone-shaped remote, Esc
 as Back

Four things v0 could not do.

Sign-in: a wrong password answered a form POST with 401 JSON, which left the
browser on a page of JSON with no way back. A form failure is now a 303 to
/login?e=<code>, and the page turns that code into a sentence from a fixed
table it owns. fetch() callers still get the same JSON they did.

Quick launch: platforms.py is a catalogue of streaming services (alias, label,
candidate packages); the browser names an alias and never a package. Netflix,
Disney+, Prime Video, YouTube and HBO Max ship on; Settings has a checkbox for
every entry, stored server-side in prefs.json as aliases only. A service with
several package names is tried candidate by candidate, best first, capped at
three attempts.

The remote: one responsive layout rather than a second mobile site. A 3x3 pad
with Back, Home, Menu and Play in the corners, then volume and search, then the
rest in groups that collapse on a phone. 44px+ targets, dark mode, no
horizontal scroll at 390px.

Esc: forwarded as KEYCODE_BACK. Releasing the keyboard is Shift+Esc, the
Release button, or clicking away. The button no longer hides itself while idle,
which used to make it vanish between mousedown and click.

Also fixes a class-name collision: key tiles carried a bare group class ("nav"),
so the header's .nav layout applied to them and scrambled the pad.

